                  "explanation": "The standard .xlsx format does not support macros. When you save a macro-containing workbook as .xlsx, Excel removes all VBA code, usually with only a brief warning that is easy to dismiss. To preserve macros you must save as a Macro-Enabled Workbook (.xlsm) or the binary .xlsb format via Save As to Save as type.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WHY THE MACRO VANISHED</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Wrong file format strips the code</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"210\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">Workbook</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"330\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">with a macro</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">FormatReport</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Ready to save</text><path d=\"M370 360 L470 360\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"470,360 453,349 453,371\" fill=\"#ef4444\"/><text x=\"420\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"18\">Save .xlsx</text><rect x=\"490\" y=\"210\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"640\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">.xlsx FILE</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cannot hold</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">any macros</text><text x=\"640\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Code removed</text><path d=\"M800 360 L900 360\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"900,360 883,349 883,371\" fill=\"#888\"/><rect x=\"830\" y=\"260\" width=\"210\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(136,136,136,0.15)\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"935\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">Reopen:</text><text x=\"935\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">no macro</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"560\" width=\"800\" height=\"230\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE FIX</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"670\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Save As to Save as type to</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"712\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Excel Macro-Enabled Workbook (.xlsm)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Then the code survives every save and reopen</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"830\" width=\"900\" height=\"70\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">No .xlsm means no macros, ever</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Saving as .xlsx strips macros; .xlsm preserves them"
                  }
